closure following partial nephrectomy</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1997</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>526</fpage><lpage>527</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9224339</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>FB</given-names></name><name><surname>Baumgartner</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Robin</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrett</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Absorbable mesh splenorrhaphy for severe splenic injuries: functional studies in an animal model and an additional patient series</article-title><source>J Trauma</source><year>1991</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>200</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1847221</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosato</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>NN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dexon mesh splenorrhaphy for intraoperative splenic injuries</article-title><source>Am Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>176</fpage><lpage>180</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12641363</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goes</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Periareolar mammaplasty: double skin technique with application of polyglactine or mixed mesh</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1996</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>959</fpage><lpage>968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8618999</pub-